      "approach": "Full session. 1 data agent fetched 15 real datasets (pinned windows); 3 framework agents (React, Vue, Svelte) each built the same 26 scenarios in a fresh Vite app linked to the monorepo build, plus framework probes (StrictMode, SSR import, reactive proxies, in-place mutation, packaging, strict type-check). Tech lead re-checked P0/P1 claims, ran pixel compares in the default and zoom states, filed issues.",
      "notes": [
        "Per-team data adapters caused most default-render pixel diffs; next full session starts with shared adapters (test/dogfood/shared/scenarios/<id>.ts).",
        "The default-render compare is a contract check; the zoom state caught the wrapper bug (a 0.32% diff in axis labels).",
        "Two teams found the same core bug independently: overlap across frameworks is cheap verification.",
        "Teams graded the same bug differently (OK vs BUG); the brief now says any attached finding means BUG.",
        "Svelte 5 blocked the runes probes; they stay unrun until it works."
